  "notes": {
    "habelia": "Aria and Caron2017 Fig1 actual fossils personally inspected, separating morphA panelsD-G from morphB. Fig3 morphA anatomical drawing inspected as interpretation, not fossil. Use H.optata morphA holotypeUSNM57693 and ROMIP64359. Actual text specifies12trunk segments, five thoracic limb pairs and posterior exopods6-12: seven posterior segments, despite inconsistent family diagnosis eight. Bipartite telson near head+trunk length; five gnathobase/raptorial cephalic pairs plus reduced anterior pair and intermediary pair.2018correction read; Thelxiope seven-tergite correction does not change Habelia. Color and detailed proportions artistic.",
    "alalcomenaeus": "ROM45616 and holotypeUSNM155658 actual fossils personally inspected. Eleven trunk tergites, enclosing pleurae, broad unpaired spatulate telson with posterior spines and compact three-ramus flagellate frontal appendages. Primary BriggsCollins1999 abstract read, documenting historical fifth-eye claim. Aria etal2015 DOI10.1111/pala.12161 Eyes section read: fifth Alalcomenaeus eye evidence unclear; paired mushroom median eyes likely leanchoiliid state. Adopt two lateral plus two median eyes with explicit unresolved fossil interpretation, not claimed proven absence of fifth. Leanchoilia USNM155648 fossil comparator personally inspected: pointed lanceolate tail, extended frontal peduncles. No CNS modeling.",
    "plenocaris": "ROM61125 and USNM57700 actual fossils personally inspected. Short anterior carapace, long ringed posterior region and paired broad terminal paddles readable. Museum primary collection description specifies13abdominal segments,2-4legpairs and approximately10antenna segments with ventral spines; detailed head/limbs acknowledged poorly resolved. Use3simple legpairs as bounded choice, no transplanted Yohoia raptorial appendages. Whittington1974 DOI lookup did not yield fullpaper; do not claim it personally read. PerspicarisROM61111 actual comparator inspected: extended oval carapace with10thoracic segments and7abdominal, narrow forked tail; Plenocaris paired broad paddles/13exposedabdomen is structural distinction not scale-only.",
    "nectocaris": "Vinther2025 fullpaper local PDF and diagnosis/discussion personally read; Fig6 N.pteryxROM59660G-I and ROM59661J-N pixels personally inspected, not N.latusA-F or schematicO/P as specimen. ROM59658 and59660 external fossils personally inspected. Flat elongated kite trunk with continuous lateral ray-bearing fins, narrow eyed head, paired sensory antennae, flared tubular mouth. No separate caudal region, no Nektognathus substitution, no exposed internal jaws. Cephalopod/jet-propulsion/prehensile-arm assertions obsolete; feeding suction tentative; colors/body thickness artistic."
  },
